	<title>A Suitable Boy (A Suitable Boy, #1)</title>
	<isbn>0060786523</isbn>
	<publication_year />
	<language_code>en-US</language_code>
	<description>Vikram Seth's novel is, at its core, a love story: Lata and her mother, Mrs. Rupa Mehra, are both trying to find -- through love or through exacting maternal appraisal -- a suitable boy for Lata to marry. Set in the early 1950s, in an India newly independent and struggling through a time of crisis, &lt;i&gt;A Suitable Boy&lt;/i&gt; takes us into the richly imagined world of four large extended families and spins a compulsively readable tale of their lives and loves. A sweeping panoramic portrait of a complex, multi ethnic society in flux, &lt;i&gt;A Suitable Boy&lt;/i&gt; remains the story of ordinary people caught up in a web of love and ambition, humor and sadness, prejudice and reconciliation, the most delicate social etiquette and the most appalling violence.</description>
